# Soft and Chewy Oatmeal Raisin Cookies

Based on [Sally’s Baking Addiction](https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/soft-chewy-oatmeal-raisin-cookies)

{ rating="0" image="soft_chewy_oatmeal_raisin_cookies.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 cup (2 sticks; 226g) [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, softened to room temperature
- [ ] 1 cup (200g) [packed light]{ ing="packed-light" } or dark brown sugar
- [ ] 1/4 cup (50g) [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }
- [ ] 2 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [pure vanilla extract]{ ing="pure-vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp (15ml) [unsulphured or dark molasses]{ ing="unsulphured-or-dark-molasses" }
- [ ] 1.67 cups (209g) [all-purpose flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" } (spooned & leveled)
- [ ] 1 tsp [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [ground cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 3 cups (255g) [old-fashioned whole rolled oats]{ ing="old-fashioned-whole-rolled-oats" }
- [ ] 1 cup (140g) [raisins]{ ing="raisins" }
- [ ] [Optional: 1/2 cup]{ ing="optional-1-2-cup" } (64g) chopped toasted walnuts

## Recipe

1. Cream softened [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" } and both [sugars]{ ing="granulated-sugar" } together on medium speed until smooth, about 3 minutes. Add [eggs]{ ing="egg" } and mix on high for 1 minute. Scrape bowl as needed. Add vanilla and [molasses]{ ing="unsulphured-or-dark-molasses" }, mixing on high until combined
1. In a separate bowl, whisk [flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }, [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }, [cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" }. Add to wet ingredients on low speed. Beat in [oats]{ ing="old-fashioned-whole-rolled-oats" }, [raisins]{ ing="raisins" }, and walnuts on low speed. Chill dough 30-60 minutes in refrigerator
1. Preheat oven to 350F (177C). Line two baking sheets with parchment paper or silicone mats
1. Roll dough into 2-Tbsp balls, spacing 2 inches apart. Bake 12-14 minutes until lightly browned on sides. Centers will appear soft. Cool on sheet for 5 minutes, then transfer to wire rack to cool completely

## Notes

- Using a cookie scoop helps manage sticky dough
- Cookies continue to set on the baking sheet during the cooling period
- Also see the main cookie recipe: [Chocolate Chip Cookies](./chocolate_chip_cookies.html)
- Other oatmeal cookie variations: [Chocolate Chip Oatmeal Cookies](./chocolate_chip_oatmeal_cookies.html), [Dark Chocolate Cranberry Oatmeal Cookies](./dark_chocolate_cranberry_oatmeal_cookies.html)
